<section class="seo-content" id="how-to-play" aria-labelledby="seo-heading">
  <div class="seo-inner">
    <h2 id="seo-heading">How to play Snake Game</h2>

    <p>
      Snake Game is the classic arcade game of growing a snake on a square board. You steer the snake
      toward the fruit; every fruit you eat adds a segment and scores points. The board never grows,
      so the longer you get, the harder every turn becomes — hit a wall or your own tail and the run
      is over.
    </p>

    <h3>Controls</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Steer:</strong> arrow keys or W / A / S / D.</li>
      <li><strong>Start, pause, resume:</strong> Space.</li>
      <li><strong>Pause:</strong> P (the game also pauses when the tab loses focus).</li>
      <li><strong>Restart:</strong> R, or Play again on the results screen.</li>
      <li><strong>On touch screens:</strong> swipe on the board or tap the direction pad.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Four ways to play</h3>
    <p>
      Pick the mode that suits you. Each mode keeps its own best score and best length, saved on your
      device.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Classic</strong> — the original rules. Eat fruit, grow, and don't hit the wall or
        your own tail.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Time Attack</strong> — 60 seconds on the clock. Same rules as Classic, but the clock
        is your opponent.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Zen</strong> — walls wrap around. Leave one edge and you appear on the other; only
        your own tail can end the run.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Daily</strong> — a seeded challenge for your local calendar day. Fruit never spawns on
        the snake, so the board always stays winnable. Complete the day's 60 fruits to keep your
        streak alive.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Why this version</h3>
    <p>
      It runs instantly in your browser — no download, no login, no ads, no account. Play on desktop,
      tablet, or phone, and your scores, daily best, and streak are saved on your device. The game
      pauses when you switch tabs, and you can share a score or your daily result when a run ends.
    </p>

    <h3>Frequently asked questions</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Is there a leaderboard?</strong> No. Scores are stored only in your browser's local
        storage, so every player competes against their own best.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What is the Daily challenge?</strong> One seeded 60-fruit run per local calendar day.
        The same date always produces the same starting board and fruit sequence, and the challenge
        resets at midnight in your timezone.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Does it work offline?</strong> Yes. Everything — the game, the scores, and the daily
        challenge — runs in your browser with no network requests after the page loads.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What happens to my scores if I clear my browser data?</strong> They are stored in your
        browser's local storage, so clearing site data resets them.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>A few tips</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Leave room to turn — don't trail too closely behind yourself.</li>
      <li>Stay near the middle early on, so you have space in every direction.</li>
      <li>Near the walls, plan two or three moves ahead instead of reacting.</li>
      <li>When it gets tense, pause and think.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

